      "message": "fix(sim): a chamfer or deburr owns its declared edge break\n\nThe program sim judged the bevel a 2D Chamfer or Deburr exists to cut\nagainst the model's sharp edge, so the post gate refused every one.\n\nThe chamfer and deburr generators now declare the break they were asked\nto cut (cl::EdgeBreak: the edge, the bevel depth and slope from the op's\nown parameters, not from the moves). After deviate, the program sim\nre-judges a gouge column inside a declared break's width against the\nbevel: down to it is clean, deeper is still a gouge charged at its\nexcess, and an undeclared edge keeps the model's verdict. The record\npersists as an additive `breaks` key in the cached path.\n\nThe deburr also stops riding edges steeper than its cone's flank: a\nvertical cone on a vertical corner countersank it to the window floor\n(9.8 mm on the default brick), a real gouge. It skips them with a note.\n\nFixes #303\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
